  },
  "implementation": [
    "Optional constructed record_https endpoint uses actual native certificate/key, verifies configured server name, supports only HTTP/1.1 and binds a bounded ephemeral Core registry before native intake. Handshakes and downloads have bounded independent admission.",
    "Registry stores locator/view metadata only. Every GET authenticates a fresh current bearer, derives original Session/Participant/Connection source authority under one held Store read and checks exact viewer, revision, body/manifest binding and projected hash through Core. Restart loses references; stop invalidates registry and wakes owned IO.",
    "Closing raw application/vcon+json response owns original source/record guards and capacity through actual TLS flush/socket IO. Timers bound credential, reference and maximum30-second lifetimes; cancellation/retirement stops remaining IO.",
    "Native SDK uses original TLS pin/name/IP and current verified refresh credential. HTTP SDK requires explicit RecordTlsConfig. Both reject alternate origins, user information, query/fragment, ambiguous token paths, proxy/redirect/system-root fallback and inconsistent literal IP names. Downloads share original fetch/auth/key/reference bounds and16MiB limit, with exact UTF8 digest/schema/UUID/condition checks."
  ],
